# The Clerk at a Desk for Two

## Turning Librarian into a working desk: what we designed, what we learned, and where the problems are

**Document class:** `theory.paper` (internal development report)
**Status:** Draft 01. Internal. Retrospective theory with typed evidence. Not law, not a kernel page, not an implementation specification.
**Author and Director:** Matthew John Fisher
**Drafting support:** Claude (model `claude-opus-5-5`), an AI system made by Anthropic, working under the author's direction
**Date:** 2026-10-17
**Period covered:** 2026-10-15 to 2026-10-17
**Program:** Workshop / Librarian / Clerk / Sequence Addressing
**Parents:** *Sequence Addressing, Fractal Autonomy, and Protected Promotion* (Draft 03, 2026-09-23); *Weekend Report: Librarian / SeqAddr / Prime Autonomy* (2026-10-07)

> **Confidential.** This is an internal document of Matthew John Fisher. It is not for publication or distribution. It may be kept as a dated record of authorship.

> **Central claim:** The clerk is the desk. Two intelligences sit at it, the Director and the prime. The clerk does the mechanical part on call, so each intelligence can do what it does best, and anything that breaks the design is kicked back.

